    "wp.introduction.h2": "Introduction",
    "wp.introduction.kicker": "&sect;01 &middot; Introduction",
    "wp.introduction.p1": "Real-world assets moving on-chain today generally rely on off-chain custody with an on-chain claim layered on top of it &mdash; a bridge of trust rather than a proof. Holders are asked to believe an attestation instead of verifying one. That gap is tolerable for low-stakes use cases; it is not tolerable for institutional capital.",
    "wp.introduction.p2": "Sectora starts from a different premise: verification should be a primitive of the network, not a feature bolted onto it after the fact. Custody, attestation, and settlement are handled by infrastructure designed for that single purpose, rather than shared with unrelated general-purpose activity.",
    "wp.introduction.quote": "The question &ldquo;is this asset actually backed?&rdquo; has a cryptographic answer &mdash; not an institutional one.",
