    "wp.network.h2": "Layer 3 Architecture",
    "wp.network.kicker": "&sect;02 &middot; The Sectora Network",
    "wp.network.p1": "Sectora runs as a Layer 3 network, settling above a general-purpose base layer to inherit its security and finality while executing custody and verification logic in an environment purpose-built for that workload. Separating the execution layer from general-purpose blockspace means custody attestations never compete for throughput with unrelated activity, and the verification logic that matters most to institutional users can evolve independently of base-layer governance.",
    "wp.network.p2": "The network is currently <strong>live on testnet</strong>, open to validators, security researchers, and early integration partners ahead of its mainnet launch.",
    "wp.protocol.h2": "The Sectora Protocol",
    "wp.protocol.kicker": "&sect;03 &middot; Verification &amp; Custody",
    "wp.protocol.p1": "The Sectora Protocol is the network's verification layer: native infrastructure to audit, protect, and tokenize real-world assets through cryptographic verification, distributed custody, and institutional-grade security by design.",
    "wp.protocol.p2": "Custodied assets are represented on-chain only after passing through a verification cycle &mdash; an auditable process that ties the on-chain instrument to its off-chain backing at defined intervals, rather than at issuance alone. The result is a continuously-verifiable claim rather than a one-time attestation, giving holders and counterparties a live cryptographic record instead of a static certificate.",
    "wp.roadmap.kicker": "&sect;12 &middot; Roadmap",
